{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["Here Rashi explained: there are eleven 'cursed' statements here, corresponding to the eleven tribes; and corresponding to Simeon no curse was written, because it was not in His heart to bless him. The reason: because in the affair of Peor they were together with their prince, Zimri son of Salu, in a matter that was not for the sake of Heaven. And according to this line, 'cursed be the one who does not uphold' is not counted among the number, because it applies equally to all. And one may say: twelve curses, corresponding to the twelve tribes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:26.826637469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}